ges.","factors":[{"id":"atc_communication_error","role":"contributing","evidence":"[Accident] At 1:13 pm (local time), air traffic controllers in Medan cleared Flight 152 for an ILS approach to Runway 5 from its 316 degree heading."},{"id":"gpws_warning_response","role":"contributing","evidence":"Contributing to the accident was the failure of the Ground Proximity Warning System (GPWS) for undetermined reasons and the inadequate vectoring charts used by the controllers at Medan."},{"id":"inadequate_training","role":"contributing","evidence":"The two pilots aboard the accident flight were qualified to fly both the FFCC and the -600 model, however the adequacy of their conversion training between the two would later be called into question."},{"id":"loss_of_situational_awareness","role":"contributing","evidence":"The First Officer was distracted during the turn and did not notice for a while that the aircraft was turning left."},{"id":"low_visibility","role":"contributing","evidence":"This led to the controller mistakenly saying \"Merpati one five two turn left heading 240 to intercept runway zero five from the right side\"; as the wrong call sign was used, the Garuda pilots disregar"},{"id":"manufacturer_communication","role":"contributing","evidence":"On 26 September 1997, the Airbus A300 flying the route crashed into mountainous woodlands near the village of Buah Nabar, Sibolangit, killing all 222 passengers and 12 crew members on board."},{"id":"operator_safety_culture","role":"contributing","evidence":"Air traffic controllers then became confused as to which plane they were talking to, as another flight with the same number (Merpati Nusantara Airlines Flight 152) was also in the area at the time."},{"id":"pilot_experience","role":"contributing","evidence":"The crew, led by Captain Hance Rachmo Wiyogo (41), a pilot with 19 years of flying experience at Garuda Indonesia and nearly 12,000 flying hours, and First Officer Tata Zuwaldi (also 41), a former fli"},{"id":"